{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530149-vda20-sarapion","id":1530149,"title":"VDA20 Sarapion?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-07T03:24:31-08:00","id":1530149,"title":"VDA20 Sarapion?","content":"Hello there!<br /> <br /> VDA20 Companion mentions an ancient Laibon under Mogadishu by the name of Sarapion. Overall, not a lot of info is given on him, though he seems like a big guy, laughing at both Caine and Set.<br /> <br /> Is there any other info on him somewhere?<br /> <br /> The only thing that comes to my mind to link him to pre-existing lore is to connect him to Archduke Azrael, but that only fits to some extent.<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T03:53:00-08:00","id":1530150,"title":"","content":"Are you certain Sarapion is male?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T04:40:09-08:00","id":1530152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530149-vda20-sarapion?p=1530150#post1530150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you certain Sarapion is male?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm not, but I had first thought the name had to do with the Hellenistic Serapis, who is depicted as male, and in my mind it stuck that way. I just discovered it that Sarapion is the ancient name of Mogadishu, but I wouldn't necessarily be surprised to find it is etymologically related to Serapis, though it's just an UNeducated guess.<br /> Also, just checked: the Companion uses &quot;it&quot; as pronoun for Sarapion, but I hadn't noticed.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T04:45:12-08:00","id":1530153,"title":"","content":"Well, afaik <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarapion\" target=\"_blank\">Sarapion</a> is simply the name of a port city that might or not have been Mogadishu's precursor or at least an ancient neighbor.<br /> <br /> The fact the name per se seems to be a variant of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serapion\" target=\"_blank\">Serapion</a>, that could have originated from Seraphim or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serapeum\" target=\"_blank\">something else altogether</a>, makes that &quot;laughing at both Caine and Set&quot; assertion sound questionable at best. Put those things together and it all looks like perhaps the product of myth-making narratives by much younger (relatively speaking) local kindred.<br /> <br /> Not saying there <b>couldn't</b> be some ancient Laibon sleeping under the close vicinity of Mogadishu and that he/she/it might recognize no Caine or Set as ancestor. But at minimum i strongly doubt that name would truly be its own.<br /> <br /> Just my two cents of thought.<br /> <br /> <br /> Little aside, what <b>else </b>does VDA20 Companion tell us about medieval Mogadishu and the walking corpses that inhabit on the shadows of its people?<br /> I'm curious now about what other tidbits to help a ST in starting a version of the city the book does offer us.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though the idea of a city - or several cities in the sultanate (be it of Mogadishu or Ajuran) divided across &quot;cainite&quot;, &quot;setite&quot; and &quot;laibon&quot; clique/culture/faction lines, with possible subdivisions &amp; disputes around groups with conflicting definitions of &quot;cainite&quot; (what if some kindred conflate Set the egyptian god with, Seth, 3rd son of Adam?), &quot;setite&quot; or &quot;laibon&quot; (that have varied immensely in presentation between editions), more than a few of them looking for some elusive ancestor/ancient that will prove them right &amp;/or destroy their rivals, could in itself provide plenty of strife. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-01-2024, 05:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T09:54:12-08:00","id":1530181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530149-vda20-sarapion?p=1530152#post1530152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I'm not, but I had first thought the name had to do with the Hellenistic Serapis, who is depicted as male, and in my mind it stuck that way. I just discovered it that Sarapion is the ancient name of Mogadishu, but I wouldn't necessarily be surprised to find it is etymologically related to Serapis, though it's just an UNeducated guess.<br /> Also, just checked: the Companion uses &quot;it&quot; as pronoun for Sarapion, but I hadn't noticed.<br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-07T15:38:39-08:00","id":1530213,"title":"","content":"Took a look into VDA20 Companion - the book says a lot about the region might be said, 15 pages packed of imagery and plot seeds for STs and players to riff, kitbash and develop to taste - and it seems to indicate Sarapion adopted its current name in jest/reference to the city built over its resting place, pretty much implying a role as shadow founder and being <b><i>already </i></b>ancient between the first to third centuries, supposed time of writing of some of the better known works to cite the port city, like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geography_(Ptolemy)\" target=\"_blank\">Ptolemy's Geography</a> and the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Periplus_of_the_Erythraean_Sea\" target=\"_blank\">Periplus of the Erythraean Sea</a>.<br /> <br /> Text also makes quite clear that truth of identity aside, the ancient is very much real and <b>NOT</b> a product of kindred historical romanticism/revisionism as i had suggested as an alternative.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also ended up bumping into a little unrelated morsel that i found most curious indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bantu \u2014 (Eleventh Generation Impundulu) and Esihle \u2014 (Bomkazi Witch) This husband-wife team has been together since they were babes. Their mothers raised the children together, fully expecting both of them to take up the mantle of the Bomkazi witches. For Bantu, magic never took, and the Impundulu chose him to join their ranks beyond death instead. The pair left their home in the Cape to seek an answer to the Impundulu\u2019s plight, and believe they found it with an elder of the children of Cagn.<br /> They first encountered this creature, ancient and steeped in death, on the Swahili coast <i>where locals named it \u201c<b>devourer of human flesh</b>\u201d or \u201c<b>Mla Watu</b>.\u201d</i> Mla Watu abandoned them before they learned everything they needed to, but they have since tracked it further north to Ceel Waaq and finally, Mogadishu. </div> </div> </div>You know guys, that doesn't sound very Cappadocian at all. Quite <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nagaraja_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">something else</a> in fact....<br /> <br /> (That said in my own current game the Impundulu &amp; Bomkazi are something quite separate from the Mla Watu and still very much around in contemporary times, having found <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dhampir_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">workarounds</a> or perhaps more precisely, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Thin-Blood_Alchemy\" target=\"_blank\">solutions</a>, to deal with their past difficulties)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-01-2024, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T08:44:30-08:00","id":1530379,"title":"","content":"Honestly, someone <i>really </i>needs to do something about that spam filter - or at least have someone to check into its shenanigans more regularly - second post thrown into limbo because i <b>dared </b>to edit stuff.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, some more thoughts and ramblings on the topic's subject after skimming back &amp; forth through the chapter on the Domain of Mogadishu:<br /> <br /> - The Children of Sarapion's inability to impede the takeover by the Ramanga and indeed their success in keeping the reins of power for half a millenium, before Farnaza's own rise to rulership with the support of Assamites and local muslim kindred, seems to hint that pretensions aside, Sarapion might not be much more potent than Arawelo and indeed a 5th generation just like the warrior-queen. The fact that even after her fall and self-exile, Sarapion appears much more interested in sabotaging the efforts of her childe Mazigha in reclaiming power than advancing its own position or asserting control over the current Na'ib, seems to reinforce this idea the Ramanga might be a little too close for confort.<br /> <br /> - I strongly suspect that, title notwithstanding, the Children of Sarapion are more of a personality cult than the ancient's literal brood. Its openess to accepting all Laibon irrespective of lineage and absence of any leadership figure outside of hearsay, legend and rumor around the figure of their elusive &quot;founder&quot; seems to go a long way in supporting such a interpretation of the status quo.<br /> <br /> - Sarapion shows the signs of an Osiris through and through and its methodology appears to point to an individual with high levels of Obfuscate or Presence, if not both, what alongside its apparent lack of childer and opposition to the worship of any divine figure beside itself, can rise some <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Baali\" target=\"_blank\">peculiar thoughts</a> about its particular <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ministry_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">lineage</a>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, the matter of the two mosques, the mayhem around support and sabotage of their construction, the issue of spiritual miasma resulting of the politic-religious disputes and its peculiar effects on the practicioners of a variety of Roads seems most interesting indeed. It brings all kinds of questions and potential for trouble to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-03-2025, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T10:57:22-08:00","id":1530391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530149-vda20-sarapion?p=1530379#post1530379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, someone <i>really </i>needs to do something about that spam filter - or at least have someone to check into its shenanigans more regularly - second post thrown into limbo because i <b>dared </b>to edit stuff.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, some more thoughts and ramblings on the topic's subject after skimming back &amp; forth through the chapter on the Domain of Mogadishu:<br /> <br /> - The Children of Sarapion's inability to impede the takeover by the Ramanga and indeed their success in keeping the reins of power for half a millenium, before Farnaza's own rise to rulership with the support of Assamites and local muslim kindred, seems to hint that pretensions aside, Serapion might not be much more potent than Arawelo and indeed a 5th generation just like the warrior-queen. The fact that even after her fall and self-exile, Sarapion appears much more interested in sabotaging the efforts of her childe Mazigha in reclaiming power than advancing its own position or asserting control over the current Na'ib, seems to reinforce this idea the Ramanga might be a little too close for confort.<br /> <br /> - I strongly suspect that, title notwithstanding, the Children of Sarapion are more of a personality cult than the ancient's literal brood. Its openess to accepting all Laibon irrespective of lineage and absence of any leadership figure outside of hearsay, legend and rumor around the figure of their elusive &quot;founder&quot; seems to go a long way in supporting such a interpretation of the status quo.<br /> <br /> - Sarapion shows the signs of an Osiris through and through and its methodology appears to point to an individual with high levels of Obfuscate or Presence, if not both, what alongside its apparent lack of childer and opposition to the worship of any divine figure beside itself, can rise some <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Baali\" target=\"_blank\">peculiar thoughts</a> about its particular <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ministry_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">lineage</a>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, the matter of the two mosques, the mayhem around support and sabotage of their construction the issue of spiritual miasma resulting of the politic-religious disputes and its peculiar effects on the practicioners of a variety of Roads seems most interesting indeed. It brings all kinds of questions and potential for trouble to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about a Setite lineage, unless it's an ancient Warrior of Glycon or Witch of Echidna who has reasons not to be too fond of or impressed by Set. I do suspect Azrael because in the lore of previous editions he was an earthbound in the kingdom of Kush, which is not really Mogadishu, but is also not too far. Or he may be an elder Baali, as you suggest. Seen as the Ramanga derive their powers from a creature of the Abyss, there may be competition between that creature and Sarapion or his infernal/abyssal masters (isn't the abyss where the Fallen are trapped?). The disdain for both Caine and Set might point to a vampire inked to Lilith, too, or potentially from a new, unknown lineage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T18:19:18-08:00","id":1530414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530149-vda20-sarapion?p=1530391#post1530391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure about a Setite lineage, unless it's an ancient Warrior of Glycon or Witch of Echidna who has reasons not to be too fond of or impressed by Set. I do suspect Azrael because in the lore of previous editions he was an earthbound in the kingdom of Kush, which is not really Mogadishu, but is also not too far. Or he may be an elder Baali, as you suggest. Seen as the Ramanga derive their powers from a creature of the Abyss, there may be competition between that creature and Sarapion or his infernal/abyssal masters (isn't the abyss where the Fallen are trapped?). The disdain for both Caine and Set might point to a vampire inked to Lilith, too, or potentially from a new, unknown lineage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly i was thinking of no lineage in particular when i mentioned Setite, i just went with what seemed to fit with the package and a rogue Setite that forsook the founder could work, though Baali could cover such bases just as well if not better, since there seems to be a theme of clashes of faith on several levels to the chapter, what is then brought to another scale with the weird doings of kindred &amp; mortals and the buildup of colateral in the &quot;One Masjid Too Many - a Slaughter of Builders&quot; adventure seed.<br /> <br /> It can raises even more questions depending who or what \u201cSarapion who Dwells Beneath\u201d is supposed to mean in that context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}